CursorWindow JNI: @CriticalNative grouping of the method table (the
android_database_CursorWindow.cpp part of an upstream commit only)

Upstream: platform/frameworks/base commit 06b30aa5b9305c5da3368bca6c811cb3e0a12be9
  "Update @CriticalNative usage for framework methods"
  Author Jared Duke, 2025-07-25. Change-Id I9270f90cca024b2fa2689b7a41cab60d016ee9d6, Bug 374158990.
  First tagged in android-16.0.0_r4 (not in r1, r2 or r3).
Diff fetched from
  https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/06b30aa5b9305c5da3368bca6c811cb3e0a12be9%5E%21/
  and reduced to its core/jni/android_database_CursorWindow.cpp hunks, which
  are unchanged. The other files of the commit are left out: android_os_Trace.cpp
  and android_tracing_PerfettoDataSource.cpp are not built for the host, and
  the android_util_Binder.cpp hunk changes neither code nor table order there.

Why: prerequisite of 0003 (a86bb7e464 is written against this version of
the file), and it is what the official library has. On the host
CRITICAL_JNI_PARAMS_COMMA expands to "JNIEnv*, jclass," (core_jni_helpers.h),
so the functions are unchanged; the only effect is the order of the
CursorWindow JNINativeMethod table. The official library (BLR2.250402.052)
registers nativeAllocRow, nativeGetLong, nativeGetDouble, then nativeClear,
nativeGetNumRows, nativeFreeLastRow, nativeGetType, nativeSetNumColumns,
which is this commit's order (r1: nativeClear, nativeGetNumRows,
nativeSetNumColumns, nativeAllocRow, ...).

